-- Newsroom drafts for 2026-11-16 (Monday). Loaded once into EDITORIAL_REVIEW; an editor approves before anything is published.
-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or in the open 2026-11-09 draft (grepped content/ and seed/).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons were unreachable from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Library of Congress tile URLs built from resource IDs confirmed by search (Carol M. Highsmith and Bain News Service, no known restrictions). Editor: confirm each photo loads and matches its caption; the image check removes any that do not.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261116-lions-patriots', 'lions-35-patriots-10-drake-maye-ankle-injury-munich', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'nfl', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Lions 35, Patriots 10: Drake Maye leaves with an ankle injury as New England is routed in Munich', 'Detroit led 21-3 at halftime at Allianz Arena on Sunday, Nov. 15. Tommy DeVito finished at quarterback, and the 5-5 Patriots go into their bye week waiting on test results for Maye.', 'The Detroit Lions beat the New England Patriots 35-10 at Allianz Arena in Munich, Germany, on Sunday, Nov. 15, and the bigger loss for New England may have come on its opening drive. Quarterback Drake Maye hurt his ankle in the first quarter and did not return, CBS Boston reported.

## The injury

Lions defensive end Aidan Hutchinson sacked Maye on a third down and landed on his lower leg, ESPN reported. Maye was helped up, limped to the sideline and walked to the locker room. The Patriots first listed him as questionable before ruling him out. No penalty was called; NFL officiating analyst Walt Anderson said the tackle was neither a hip-drop nor a horse-collar foul, according to ESPN.

Coach Mike Vrabel said Maye could not finish the game and that more tests would show how serious the injury is. He said he did not believe Hutchinson meant to hurt Maye. Hutchinson himself hurt his right knee celebrating the sack, ESPN reported.

## How it got away

Tommy DeVito took over on the next drive. After Maye left, the Patriots punted six times, threw an interception to Roger McCreary and took a knee before halftime, CBS Boston reported. Amon-Ra St. Brown scored on catches of 56 and 28 yards, and Jahmyr Gibbs ran for two touchdowns. Detroit led 21-3 at halftime and 28-3 going into the fourth quarter. Rookie Lan Larison caught a 10-yard touchdown pass in the fourth quarter, his first in the NFL.

The Patriots'' defense did pick off Jared Goff twice, with Christian Gonzalez and Kevin Byard making the interceptions. Receiver A.J. Brown, back after missing two games with a knee injury, left in the fourth quarter with a hamstring injury, ESPN reported.

## What is next

New England fell to 5-5. The Boston Globe reported that the Patriots had entered the game holding the final AFC wild-card spot and that the game was their last before their bye week. Detroit improved to 7-2.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:63400:63421/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg', 'Ford Field, home of the Detroit Lions, in an aerial view of Detroit (file). Photo: Carol M. Highsmith / Library of Congress (highsm.63421), no known restrictions', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-16.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-16T10:50:00.000Z', '2026-11-16T10:50:00.000Z');
